AB  - Gastrointestinal (GI) disorders is a main issue in the human digestive system. Therefore, various researchers have discovered automatic detection of GI illnesses to reduce the burden on doctors and improve patient results, for either analytical or treatment purposes. The initial diagnosis and identification of GI tract illnesses, namely esophagitis, polyps, and ulcerative colitis are important for early treatment. Conventional imaging methods frequently depend on manual examination that is vulnerable to variabilities and might lack accuracy. Emerging techniques utilize traditional deep learning techniques that, however successful in the range, frequently vary from generalization and overfitting problems on medical image datasets because of the complex and small differences in disorder indication. This paper presents an Efficient Classification Of Gastrointestinal Disease Using Attention Mechanism-Based Deep Learning and Feature Engineering (ECGD-AMDLFE) model From Biomedical Images. The objective of ECGD-AMDLFE is design an efficient deep learning based approach for accurate classification of gastrointestinal disorder utilizing biomedical images. Initially, the image pre-processing stage involves dual levels, such as contrast enhancement is employed to increase the contrast of an image, and data augmentation is implemented on images. For an effective feature representation, the fusion models, namely, vision transformer, EfficientNetB7, and ShuffleNetV2, have been deployed to acquire both local and global features. Besides, the proposed ECGD-AMDLFE model designs a hybrid of convolutional bi-directional long short-term memory with attention mechanism model to accurately detect and classify gastrointestinal disease, utilizing the Nadam optimizer to enhance classification performance. A wide-range of experiment was executed to explain the performance of the ECGD-AMDLFE system. The empirical outcomes stated that the ECGD-AMDLFE methodology highlighted advancement over other existing techniques.
