AB  - Most existing Depth map Super-Resolution (DSR) methods use normal-light color images as guidance information for high-quality depth map reconstruction. However, how to at once achieve DSR and Low-light Image Enhancement (LIE) remains huge challenges. To fully excavate the merits of dual-tasks interaction learning for the LIE and DSR, this paper proposes a Joint Mutual-guidance Enhancement Network (JMENet), which mainly consists of LIE branch, DSR branch and Modal-Discrepancy Guided Self-attention (MDGS) module. Considering that the low-contrast and low-illuminance of low-light images seriously affect guidance feature extraction for DSR, we design a luminance pre-enhancement module in the LIE branch for pre-processing. To aggregate multi-scale depth features, we insert an U-shaped fusion module into the DSR branch as post-processing. To tackle color-depth structural inconsistency, both intra-modal and inter-modal differences are leveraged to build up a double-input and double-output MDGS module so as to enhance color and depth features simultaneously. Experimental results show that the proposed JMENet outperforms many advanced DSR and LIE methods for low-light color image enhancement and low-resolution depth map super-resolution. Our codes will be publicly released at: https://github.com/mdcnn/JMENet.
