KW  - Graph-level classification
KW  - Graph embedding
KW  - Graph refinement
KW  - Diffusion model
KW  - Graph kernel
AB  - Graph-level embedding methods often compute representations from the observed adjacency, which can bias learning toward purely local evidence and obscure higher-order connectivity patterns. We introduce Diffusion-Aware Graph Refinement (DAGR), a drop-in framework that refines graph topologies prior to embedding. For each graph, DAGR simulates timestamped diffusion cascades, solves a likelihood-based structural inference problem to estimate pairwise transmission rates, and constructs a sparse, weighted refinement of the topology that reveals latent long-range dependencies beyond what one-hop neighborhoods capture. We show, both theoretically and empirically, that the inferred transmission-rate matrix encodes global structural signatures, improving the detection of connectivity, bipartiteness, and triangle-freeness. Across multiple datasets and embedding methods, DAGR consistently increases graph-level classification accuracy and substantially enhances property detection on synthetic datasets.
ER  - 

