KW  - Prescribed performance
AB  - This paper investigates the trajectory tracking problem of quadrotor unmanned aerial vehicles with consideration of both attitude and position dynamics. By decoupling the overall dynamics of quadrotors into two closed loops, the trajectory tracking control problem is transformed into the command tracking control in position and attitude loops. To ensure an adjustable transient and steady-state response for the trajectory tracking errors, a prescribed performance control is utilized to guarantee the stabilization and boundedness of states. Furthermore, an observer-based robust adaptive control with performance guarantee is developed to compensate for the effect of the unknown dynamic parameters in the position loop. In the attitude loop, a novel incremental adaptive dynamic programming method is proposed to achieve adaptive optimal control without requiring system dynamics. This approach updates the parameters of the approximation functions online, which eliminates the need for an offline learning stage and enables a flexible controller design. In both control loops, lumped disturbances from the inter-channel coupling and multi-source disturbances are estimated using high-order sliding mode observers. Simulation results validate the effectiveness and superiority of the proposed control method.
